<div class="unit-details">
    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 1</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-mobile-screen-button"></i> Launch MiniPhone OS</h2>
        <p>You have been given access to a simulated smartphone running <strong>MiniPhone OS</strong>. Your job is to investigate the apps installed on it and find out exactly what data they are trying to collect about you.</p>

        <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Open the simulation and go to the <strong>Messages</strong> app.</li>
            <li>Follow the missions in the messages (one at a time).</li>
            <li>On a laptop: use the <strong>Notes</strong> panel on the right for your checklist and “Impact” (on mobile: tap <strong>Notes</strong>).</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="activity-toolbar no-print" style="margin: 1rem 0 0; justify-content: flex-start;">
            <a href="activity2/index.html" class="action-btn action-btn--primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-mobile-screen"></i>
                Launch activity
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 2</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-clipboard-list"></i> Create Your Investigation Log</h2>
        <p>Before you start, draw a simple table in your exercise book. You will fill it in as you explore each app.</p>

        <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>Table headings</strong></h3>
            <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <li>App</li>
                <li>What data did it ask for?</li>
                <li>Why might it want it?</li>
                <li>What happens if you say <strong>NO</strong>?</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>Apps to investigate</strong></h3>
            <ul class="custom-list" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <li><strong>Browser</strong> (cookies)</li>
                <li><strong>Connectify</strong> (terms & conditions)</li>
                <li><strong>MapMe</strong> (location)</li>
                <li><strong>Super Puzzle Quest</strong> (free app permissions)</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>Tip</strong></h3>
            <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <li>Use short bullet points (no long paragraphs).</li>
                <li>Use <strong>Case File</strong> and the <strong>Notes</strong> panel to see what data was collected.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 3</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i> Complete the Missions</h2>
        <p>Follow the instructions in the <strong>Messages</strong> app. Work through one mission at a time. Keep notes in your investigation log. Use <strong>Case File</strong> to see what data was collected.</p>

        <div class="grid-2-col" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>Browser</strong> (Cookies)</h3>
                <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li>Try both: <strong>Accept all cookies</strong> and <strong>Essential only</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Tap a few items. Does the <strong>Sponsored</strong> section change?</li>
                    <li>What changes about the ads you see?</li>
                    <li>Use the cookie button to change your choice and try again.</li>
                    <li>Record what data might be collected if you accept all.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>Connectify</strong> (Terms)</h3>
                <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li>Tap the <strong>highlighted clauses</strong> in the Terms & Conditions.</li>
                    <li>Decide: would you agree or decline? Why?</li>
                    <li>If you agree: explore the tabs and look for “Sponsored” content.</li>
                    <li>Record what the app might do with your data.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>MapMe</strong> (Location)</h3>
                <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li>Try both: <strong>Precise</strong> and <strong>Approximate</strong> location.</li>
                    <li>Tap the pins on the map. Compare the dot vs the big circle.</li>
                    <li>Does the app still work without your exact location?</li>
                    <li>Use the crosshair button to change your location choice.</li>
                    <li>Record the privacy benefit of approximate location.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>Super Puzzle Quest</strong> (Free app)</h3>
                <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li>Notice what it asks for: tracking, camera, contacts.</li>
                    <li>After setup: watch one ad for coins. What do you notice?</li>
                    <li>What do you lose if you say <strong>NO</strong>?</li>
                    <li>Record why a “free” app might want your data.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 4</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i> Reflection</h2>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>A.</strong> The “greediest” app</h3>
                <p>Which app asked for the most data? Did it seem justified?</p>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>B.</strong> The trade-off</h3>
                <p>Give one example where you chose between <strong>privacy</strong> (keeping data safe) and <strong>convenience</strong> (making the app easier to use). What did you choose and why?</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 5</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-comments"></i> Partner Discussion</h2>
            <p>Compare your “Data Footprint” score with your partner. Who has more items in their footprint? Why?</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap"></i> By the end of this task, you should be able to…</h2>
        <ul class="custom-list" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li>Identify common permissions apps ask for (location, photos, tracking)</li>
            <li>Explain the trade-offs between privacy and functionality</li>
            <li>Understand that “free” apps often pay for themselves with your data</li>
            <li>Make informed choices about app permissions</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
